From: avlo-py-build <py-build@avlo.local>
Subject: [PATCH] AVLO: drop loadPackage/lockfile/micropip loader machinery

Sever the two import edges into load-package.ts (api.ts:4, types.ts:9) so
esbuild tree-shakes load-package/installer/packaging-utils out of both
bundles, then delete the lockfile plumbing in pyodide.ts: config fields
lockFileURL/lockFileContents/packageBaseUrl/packageCacheDir/cdnUrl, the
boot-time pyodide-lock.json fetch, API.lockFilePromise, and the
packageIndexReady await. AVLO artifacts mount everything explicitly
(stdLibURL + bundle tars); nothing reads a lockfile or hits a CDN, and
the package.json/pyodide-lock.json/pyodide.js boot crutch goes away.
The dead sources stay on disk but leave the tsc program (tsconfig
exclude) — the outer-bundle make rule runs `tsc --noEmit` first.
Snapshot seams (_makeSnapshot/_loadSnapshot/_snapshotDeserializer/
BUILD_ID), stdLibURL, and packages/fullStdLib stay untouched.

One survivor is re-anchored: dynload.ts was reachable only through
load-package (via installer), and its module scope attaches
API.loadDynlib plus the DSO snapshot record/replay surface (0005) —
severing the edges tree-shook it out of the glue, killing bundle
mounts and makeSnapshot. A bare side-effect import in api.ts keeps it
in the graph (src/js has no sideEffects flag, so esbuild preserves it).

